  <h2>Orientation</h2>
  <p>Labs 1 and 2 built systems that answer. This one builds a system that decides. An employee asks the assistant about leave, and it can now do three things: look the policy up, check that person's remaining balance, and file a leave request. The model chooses which, in what order, and with what arguments.</p>
  <p>That choice is the whole risk profile. A retrieval mistake produces a wrong sentence; an action mistake produces a wrong row in a system of record. Everything in this lab — the permission boundaries, the guardrail, the traces, the evaluation — exists because the model is now allowed to do things.</p>

