  <h3>Glossary</h3>
  <dl>
    <dt>Action group</dt>
    <dd>A set of operations the agent may call, described by a function schema or an OpenAPI schema, and backed by a Lambda function. The descriptions in the schema are what the model reads when deciding — they are prompt text, not documentation.</dd>
    <dt>Orchestration</dt>
    <dd>The agent's loop: read the request, decide whether to retrieve, call an action, ask a follow-up question, or answer. Bedrock exposes the default orchestration prompt for editing when you need to change how that decision is made.</dd>
    <dt>Prepare and alias</dt>
    <dd>Edits sit in a draft until you <em>prepare</em> the agent. A <em>version</em> is a frozen snapshot and an <em>alias</em> is a movable pointer at one. Applications call an alias, never the draft.</dd>
    <dt>Trace</dt>
    <dd>The step-by-step record of one invocation: the model's rationale, the retrieval it performed, the action it chose, the observations it got back. This is the only way to debug an agent that behaves oddly.</dd>
    <dt>Contextual grounding check</dt>
    <dd>A guardrail policy that scores each response for grounding in the supplied context and relevance to the query, blocking below your threshold. The specific defence against a fluent, confident, unsupported answer.</dd>
  </dl>

